  "result": "I fixed the open-bound clamping bug in `IntRange`. Clamped values now stay inside the range.\n\n**Change:** In `src/click/types.py`, `IntRange._clamp` returned `bound - dir` for open bounds. `convert` passes `dir` pointing into the range, so the subtraction moved the result outside it. It now returns `bound + dir`.\n\n**Tests:** I added two cases to `tests/test_types.py`:\n- `IntRange(0, 5, min_open=True, clamp=True)` with `\"-1\"` \u2192 `1`\n- `IntRange(0, 5, max_open=True, clamp=True)` with `\"9\"` \u2192 `4`\n\n**Results:** `python -m pytest tests/test_types.py tests/test_info_dict.py -q` gives 71 passed, 2 skipped.\n\nI didn't commit anything, and I didn't add the optional changelog entry from the plan.",
